  "findings": [
    {
      "rubric_id": "R5",
      "class": "decision-now",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "affected_surface": "section 2.8 item (3) and P1a watcher: '<live-base>/runs/paths.json' rewritten every heartbeat by each project watcher",
      "claim": "paths.json is a cross-project file but the single-writer design is per project, so two concurrent project watchers overwrite each other's entries on every heartbeat; the plan does not name this race and the mod's cwd-to-project_key resolution (step b) silently fails for whichever project heartbeated earlier.",
      "evidence": "Section 2.8 says the watcher 'rewrites <live-base>/runs/paths.json from git worktree list --porcelain each heartbeat' with the map keyed by that repo's worktree roots only; P1a says writer granularity is project and the lock is 'runs/<project_key>.lock'; nothing in section 2.5, P1a, or the runs-watch tests covers two watchers of different projects sharing paths.json. The runs-watch.test.sh case list has 'two watchers same project -> writer_busy' and 'two roots same repo' but no 'two projects, two watchers' case.",
      "evidence_reference": "section 2.8 (3); section 4 P1a 'watcher src/status/runs-watch.js' and '驗收'; section 6 row '多 session／多 root 互相覆蓋'",
      "repair": "Pick one and write it into section 2.8 and P1a: (a) per-project file 'runs/paths.<project_key>.json' written under the existing project lock, with the mod listing 'runs/paths.*.json' and taking the longest prefix across all of them (add '$.fs readdir available?' to S2); or (b) keep one global paths.json but make every rewrite a read-merge-write under a separate '<live-base>/runs/paths.lock' flock, keyed by realpath so stale entries for the same root are replaced not duplicated. Add a runs-watch.test.sh case: two fixture repos, two watchers, both heartbeat, then paths.json (or the file set) still resolves cwd of both repos to the correct project_key. Add a row to section 6.",
      "blocks_next_slice_or_immediate_integrity": true,
      "cannot_defer_to_spike": true,
      "rubric_mapped": true,
      "candidate_blocker": true,
      "provenance": [
        {
          "seat_id": "claude_architecture",
          "runner": "claude-native",
          "model": "claude-fable-5-1"
        }
      ],
