      "fingerprint": "97a17fd717512e1c539b0f4ab962d17d11d628dbc5468c4f595de683bc5a61a1"
    },
    {
      "rubric_id": "R4",
      "class": "decision-now",
      "severity": "blocking",
      "affected_surface": "section 2.8 mod resolution order and P1c register.ts: how the sandboxed mod locates '<live-base>' and '~'",
      "claim": "P1c silently depends on the mod being able to resolve the tmpfs base ('/run/user/<uid>/autopilot', uid dependent) and the home directory ('~/.autopilot/session-mode/<sid>.json', '~/.autopilot/review/...') while section 2.8 forbids the mod from reading env or running git; no spike asks how that discovery happens, so the whole band can be 'no project' on a host where the sandbox does not expose XDG_RUNTIME_DIR or HOME.",
      "evidence": "Section 2.8 states the mod resolution 'does not run git, does not read env, does not compute hash' and starts from '$.session.id()' then reads '~/.autopilot/session-mode/<sid>.json'; live-state-dir.js is described in section 2.5 as resolving the base to '/run/user/1000/autopilot' [V-run] which is uid specific. S2 asks whether these paths are readable and their sizes but not how the mod obtains the two base paths. Only '$.session.id()' and '$.session.cwd()' are marked [V-file].",
      "evidence_reference": "section 2.8 'mod 解析順序'; section 4 P0 row S2; section 2.5 live-base bullet",
      "repair": "Add to S2 an explicit question: which API gives the mod HOME and the live base (env accessor, '$.session.cwd()' only, or nothing). Add a design fallback to section 2.8 that does not need env: the CLI ('session-mode.js set' and the watcher) writes a small pointer file at a location derivable from cwd alone, e.g. '<realpath(worktree root)>/.autopilot/live-pointer.json' (gitignored, additive) containing live_base, review_root and project_key; the mod walks up from '$.fs.stat(cwd,{resolve:true}).realPath' to find it. State that if S2 shows the API exposes env, the pointer file is dropped. Mark the current assumption [SPIKE] until S2 lands.",
      "blocks_next_slice_or_immediate_integrity": true,
      "cannot_defer_to_spike": false,
      "rubric_mapped": true,
      "candidate_blocker": false,
      "provenance": [
