    {
      "rubric_id": "R2",
      "class": "implementation-spike",
      "severity": "non-blocking",
      "affected_surface": "scripts/lib/repo-identity.sh and the three dispatch rails' manifest write path",
      "claim": "The shell derivation relies on 'git rev-parse --path-format=absolute', which needs git 2.31 or newer; on older git both shell and Node print nothing and every manifest silently becomes 'project: null' with no diagnostic. The plan also assumes each rail already has a 'write_manifest' test seam, which this review checkout cannot confirm (no source tree present).",
      "evidence": "P1a: 'common=$(git -C \"$dir\" rev-parse --path-format=absolute --git-common-dir)' then '任一步失敗印空、manifest 寫 null'; manifest-repo-identity.test.sh is said to '用各 rail 的 test seam 跑到 write_manifest'. The review working directory contains only plan.md, so src/status/task-runtime.js and the three rails could not be inspected.",
      "evidence_reference": "section 4 P1a 'manifest 加 repo_identity（G1 R2）'; section 3 file map row 1",
      "repair": "Add to repo-identity.sh a one-line stderr diagnostic when rev-parse fails (so null is distinguishable from an old git), state the git minimum (2.31) in section 2.5 constraints, and add a parity fixture that stubs an old git to assert both sides yield null together. In the first P1a PR confirm whether dispatch-author.sh actually has a seam reaching manifest write; if not, add it as part of the same PR (small). No plan change needed otherwise.",
