    {
      "rubric_id": "R5",
      "class": "decision-now",
      "severity": "non-blocking",
      "affected_surface": "P3 'idle/<key>/<sid>.declared.json': declare-idle CLI writes, watcher writes superseded_by, --clear writes",
      "claim": "The declaration file has three writers (declare-idle CLI, the project watcher setting superseded_by, and --clear or session-mode set/retire), so a declare racing a supersede can lose one update; the single-writer rule in section 2.5 covers scope files and progress.json but this file is outside it and the plan does not name the race.",
      "evidence": "P3: 'autopilot status declare-idle ... → idle/<repo_key>/<sid>.declared.json {..., superseded_by: null}'; '解除：watcher 看到該 repo_identity 新 manifest → 寫 superseded_by: <run_id>；session-mode.js set／retire → superseded_by: session-mode:<level|retire>；--clear 手動'. Section 2.5 names a single writer only for scope files, progress.json and heartbeat.",
      "evidence_reference": "section 4 P3 '宣告' and '解除' bullets; section 2.5 live-projection bullet",
      "repair": "Make supersession append-only: writers other than the declarer never modify '.declared.json'; the watcher and session-mode write a sibling '<sid>.superseded.json' {by, at}, and the N02 aggregation treats a declaration as superseded when the sibling exists with at >= declared_at. All writes via tmp then rename. Add one declare-idle.test.sh case for declare and supersede within the same second.",
